soning, I'd put that likelihood well above the threshold, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm treating this as a prisoner's dilemma with the given payoffs, where both sides cooperating means two years each and both defecting means four. The two copies share a model but see different inputs, so their choices are only partly linked. I'll work out the cooperate-versus-defect threshold from that expected-value comparison.\n\nThe quiet option only comes out ahead if I think the other copy stays quiet with probability above about 5/7, or roughly 0.714. Given the same model and reasoning, I'd put that likelihood well above the threshold, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10323,"completion_tokens":719,"total_tokens":11042,"cost":0.027836,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.027836,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020646,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00719},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":338,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}